      *==============================================================
      * PICCLAUS - ILE COBOL PICTURE Clause Reference
      * Displays examples and descriptions of all COBOL PIC clauses.
      * F3=Exit, PageDown/PageUp to scroll through the list.
      *==============================================================
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PICCLAUS.
       AUTHOR.     BOB.
       DATE-WRITTEN. 2025.

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-I.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-I.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT PICSCRF
               ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-PICCLAUS
               ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
               FILE STATUS IS WS-SCR-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  PICSCRF.
       01  PICSCR-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF PICCLAUS.

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  WS-SCR-STATUS          PIC XX.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Response indicator area - 3 bytes, matching DDS listing:
      *   *IN03 = byte 1  (CA03  - F3 Exit)
      *   *IN25 = byte 2  (PAGEDOWN - scroll down)
      *   *IN26 = byte 3  (PAGEUP   - scroll up)
      * Each byte is X'F1' (on) or X'F0' (off), i.e. '1' or '0'
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-IND-AREA.
           05  WS-IND-F3          PIC X.
           05  WS-IND-PGDN        PIC X.
           05  WS-IND-PGUP        PIC X.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Scrolling state
      * WS-NEW-TOP is SIGNED so subtraction below zero works correctly
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       77  WS-TOP-LINE            PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-TOTAL-LINES         PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       77  WS-PAGE-SIZE           PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 18.
       77  WS-TOTAL-PAGES         PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       77  WS-CUR-PAGE            PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       77  WS-IDX                 PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-LINE-IDX            PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-NEW-TOP             PIC S9(3) COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-PAGE-NUM-EDIT       PIC ZZ9.
       77  WS-TOTAL-EDIT          PIC ZZ9.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Screen output work fields
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-SCR-WORK.
           05  WS-PAGENBR         PIC X(3).
           05  WS-TOTPAGES        PIC X(3).
           05  WS-MSGFLD          PIC X(25).
           05  WS-LINE            PIC X(77)
               OCCURS 18 TIMES.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Load helper: example (WS-EX, 27 chars) and description
      * (WS-DC, 50 chars) moved separately then copied as WS-LOAD
      * (77 chars) into WS-ENTRY(n).  COBOL pads shorter literals
      * with spaces on MOVE so no string continuation is needed.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-LOAD.
           05  WS-EX              PIC X(27).
           05  WS-DC              PIC X(50).

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * PIC clause data table - 60 entries of 77 chars each
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-PIC-TABLE.
           05  WS-ENTRY           PIC X(77)
               OCCURS 60 TIMES.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-SECTION SECTION.
       MAIN-PARA.
           PERFORM INIT-TABLE
           PERFORM CALC-PAGES
           PERFORM OPEN-SCREEN
           PERFORM SCROLL-LOOP UNTIL WS-IND-F3 = '1'
           PERFORM CLOSE-SCREEN
           GOBACK.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Open the workstation file
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       OPEN-SCREEN.
           OPEN I-O PICSCRF
           IF WS-SCR-STATUS NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY 'PICSCRF open failed: ' WS-SCR-STATUS
               GOBACK
           END-IF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Close the workstation file
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       CLOSE-SCREEN.
           CLOSE PICSCRF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Main interaction loop - repeat until F3 pressed
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       SCROLL-LOOP.
           PERFORM FILL-SCREEN
           PERFORM WRITE-SCREEN
           MOVE LOW-VALUE TO WS-IND-AREA
           PERFORM READ-SCREEN
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN WS-IND-F3   = '1'
                   CONTINUE
               WHEN WS-IND-PGDN = '1'
                   PERFORM PAGE-DOWN
               WHEN WS-IND-PGUP = '1'
                   PERFORM PAGE-UP
               WHEN OTHER
                   CONTINUE
           END-EVALUATE.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Page down: advance one page, stop at last page.
      * If already at bottom, show message and leave position unchanged.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       PAGE-DOWN.
           COMPUTE WS-NEW-TOP = WS-TOP-LINE + WS-PAGE-SIZE
           IF WS-NEW-TOP <= WS-TOTAL-LINES
               MOVE SPACES         TO WS-MSGFLD
               MOVE WS-NEW-TOP     TO WS-TOP-LINE
           ELSE
               MOVE '*** Already at bottom ***' TO WS-MSGFLD
           END-IF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Page up: retreat one page.
      * If already at top, show message and leave position unchanged.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       PAGE-UP.
           IF WS-TOP-LINE = 1
               MOVE '*** Already at top ***' TO WS-MSGFLD
           ELSE
               MOVE SPACES TO WS-MSGFLD
               COMPUTE WS-NEW-TOP = WS-TOP-LINE - WS-PAGE-SIZE
               IF WS-NEW-TOP >= 1
                   MOVE WS-NEW-TOP TO WS-TOP-LINE
               ELSE
                   MOVE 1 TO WS-TOP-LINE
               END-IF
           END-IF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Calculate total pages from total lines and page size
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       CALC-PAGES.
           COMPUTE WS-TOTAL-PAGES =
               (WS-TOTAL-LINES + WS-PAGE-SIZE - 1) / WS-PAGE-SIZE.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Fill the 18 screen lines from the table at WS-TOP-LINE
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       FILL-SCREEN.
           COMPUTE WS-CUR-PAGE =
               (WS-TOP-LINE + WS-PAGE-SIZE - 1) / WS-PAGE-SIZE

           MOVE WS-CUR-PAGE    TO WS-PAGE-NUM-EDIT
           MOVE WS-TOTAL-PAGES TO WS-TOTAL-EDIT
           MOVE WS-PAGE-NUM-EDIT TO WS-PAGENBR
           MOVE WS-TOTAL-EDIT    TO WS-TOTPAGES

           PERFORM VARYING WS-LINE-IDX FROM 1 BY 1
                   UNTIL WS-LINE-IDX > WS-PAGE-SIZE
               COMPUTE WS-IDX = WS-TOP-LINE + WS-LINE-IDX - 1
               IF WS-IDX <= WS-TOTAL-LINES
                   MOVE WS-ENTRY(WS-IDX) TO WS-LINE(WS-LINE-IDX)
               ELSE
                   MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE(WS-LINE-IDX)
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Write the screen record to the display file
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       WRITE-SCREEN.
           MOVE WS-PAGENBR   TO PAGENBR  OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-TOTPAGES  TO TOTPAGES OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-MSGFLD    TO MSGFLD   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(1)   TO LINE01   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(2)   TO LINE02   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(3)   TO LINE03   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(4)   TO LINE04   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(5)   TO LINE05   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(6)   TO LINE06   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(7)   TO LINE07   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(8)   TO LINE08   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(9)   TO LINE09   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(10)  TO LINE10   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(11)  TO LINE11   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(12)  TO LINE12   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(13)  TO LINE13   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(14)  TO LINE14   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(15)  TO LINE15   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(16)  TO LINE16   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(17)  TO LINE17   OF PICSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(18)  TO LINE18   OF PICSCR-REC
           WRITE PICSCR-REC FORMAT IS 'PICSCR'.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Read the screen; INDICATORS ARE receives the response
      * indicator bytes back from the display file.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       READ-SCREEN.
           READ PICSCRF FORMAT IS 'PICSCR'
               INDICATORS ARE WS-IND-AREA.

      *==============================================================
      * Load all PIC clause examples and descriptions.
      * Pattern for each entry:
      *   MOVE 'example' TO WS-EX
      *   MOVE 'description' TO WS-DC
      *   MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(n)
      * COBOL pads both WS-EX and WS-DC with spaces on MOVE.
      * No string continuation is used anywhere in this paragraph.
      *==============================================================
       INIT-TABLE.
           MOVE 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES

      *-- Alphabetic (A) --
           MOVE '--- Alphabetic (A) ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(1)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC A(10)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Letters and spaces only.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(2)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC A(2)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'State code: letters and spaces only.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(3)

      *-- Alphanumeric (X) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Alphanumeric (X) ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(4)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC X(30)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Any characters: letters, digits, symbols.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(5)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC X(1)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Single character flag or code field.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(6)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC X(80)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Full-width screen line buffer field.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(7)

      *-- Unsigned numeric (9) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Unsigned Numeric (9) ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(8)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 9(5)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Unsigned integer: 00000 to 99999.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(9)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 9(9)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Unsigned integer up to 999999999.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(10)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 9(7)V99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Unsigned: 7 integer, 2 decimal places.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(11)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 99V9' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Short form: 2 integer, 1 decimal place.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(12)

      *-- Signed numeric (S9) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Signed Numeric (S9) ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(13)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(5)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Signed integer: -99999 to +99999.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(14)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(9)V99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Signed: 9 integer + 2 decimal places.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(15)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(9)V99 COMP-3' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Packed decimal; efficient arithmetic.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(16)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(9) COMP-4' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Binary integer; good for counters.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(17)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(9) BINARY' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'BINARY is a synonym for COMP-4.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(18)

      *-- Implied decimal (V) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Implied Decimal (V) ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(19)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 9(5)V9(2)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'V marks decimal; not stored in the field.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(20)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(7)V9(4)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Signed; 7 integer, 4 decimal places.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(21)

      *-- Scaling (P) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Scaling Factor (P) ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(22)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 9(3)PPP' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Scales by 1000: stored value is nnn000.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(23)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC PPP9(3)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Scales by .001: stored value is .000nnn.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(24)

      *-- COMP-1 / COMP-2 floating point --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Float (COMP-1 / COMP-2)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(25)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(6)V9 COMP-1' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Single-precision float (4 bytes on IBM i).'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(26)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(16)V9(7) COMP-2' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Double-precision float (8 bytes on IBM i).'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(27)

      *-- COMP-5 native binary --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Native Binary (COMP-5) -' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(28)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(4) COMP-5' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Native binary; no digit-count truncation.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(29)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC S9(9) COMP-5' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Full 4-byte native integer value.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(30)

      *-- Edited: zero suppression (Z) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Zero Suppress --' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(31)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC ZZZZ9' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Suppress leading zeros; last digit always shown.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(32)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC Z(6)9.99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Suppress leading zeros with decimal point.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(33)

      *-- Edited: asterisk fill (*) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Asterisk Fill --' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(34)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC ***9.99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Fill leading positions with asterisks.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(35)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC *(6)9.99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Check-protect: asterisk fill shorthand.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(36)

      *-- Edited: fixed dollar sign ($) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Fixed Dollar ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(37)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC $ZZZ,ZZ9.99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Fixed $ with zero suppression and comma.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(38)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC $9(7).99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Fixed $ sign: always printed in output.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(39)

      *-- Edited: floating dollar sign ($$) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Floating Dollar ' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(40)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC $$(6)9.99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Dollar sign floats next to first digit.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(41)

      *-- Edited: sign symbols --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Sign Symbols ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(42)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC +ZZZ9.99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Leading +/-: displays sign of value.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(43)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC ZZZ9.99-' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Trailing minus: shows - only if negative.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(44)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC ZZZ9.99+' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Trailing +/-: shows + or - always.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(45)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC Z(7).99CR' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Trailing CR if negative, spaces if positive.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(46)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC Z(7).99DB' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Trailing DB if negative, spaces if positive.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(47)

      *-- Edited: comma and period --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Comma / Period -' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(48)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC ZZZ,ZZ9.99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Comma grouping separator; period for decimal.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(49)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 9(6),9(3).99' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Explicit comma inserted in picture string.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(50)

      *-- Edited: slash and blank (B) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Slash / Blank --' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(51)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 99/99/9999' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Slash inserts / in output for date display.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(52)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 9(4)B9(2)B9(2)' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'B inserts a blank space in output position.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(53)

      *-- Edited: zero insertion (0) --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Edited: Zero Insertion -' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(54)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE 'PIC 999099' TO WS-EX
           MOVE '0 inserts a literal zero digit in output.'
               TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(55)

      *-- Level 66 RENAMES --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Level 66 RENAMES ------' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(56)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '66 NEWNAME RENAMES OLDNAME' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Alias for a range of existing fields.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(57)

      *-- Level 88 condition names --
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '--- Level 88 Conditions ---' TO WS-EX
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(58)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '88 FLAG-ON VALUE ''Y''' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Condition name: true when field = Y.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(59)
           ADD 1 TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           MOVE '88 IS-DONE VALUE ''Y'' ''D''' TO WS-EX
           MOVE 'Multiple values for one condition name.' TO WS-DC
           MOVE WS-LOAD TO WS-ENTRY(60).

       END PROGRAM PICCLAUS.

